// The shared HtmlSanitizer engine, built ONCE for the whole monorepo.
//
// Output: target/core/lib/libhtmlsanitizer.so — every binding's .tests.ae deps
// this node and then links (cgo/NIF/ccall) or loads (ctypes/Fiddle/koffi/
// FFM/uFFI, via HTMLSANITIZER_LIB) that single artifact.
//
// Source: core/embed.ae (the aether_hs_embed_* C ABI) imports the local
// `htmlsanitizer` module (core/htmlsanitizer.ae) — the WHOLE sanitizer
// (HTML5 tokenizer, DOM, CSS parser, URL resolver, allow-lists) is PURE
// AETHER. The only C is core/_embed_support.c: the caller-owned-string
// bridge and the callback trampolines, linked via --extra.
//
// No caps(): the sanitizer is a pure string->string transform. It touches no
// filesystem, no network, no OS. That is a security property worth keeping —
// if this ever needs caps("fs"), something has gone wrong.
//
// aether.shared_lib publishes the whole native-lib wiring set for us —
// shared_lib, shared_library, ldlibdeps and
// shared_library_deps_including_transitive. The last two are what lib/java
// (-Djava.library.path) and lib/go (LD_LIBRARY_PATH) read, so a JVM or Go
// consumer that deps this node finds the .so with NO path plumbing in its
// leaf. Until this builder landed we hand-published those names ourselves,
// guessing at an internal contract; now the builder owns it.

import build
import aether
import aether (source, extra_source, output)

aeb(cap) {
    b = build.start()
    aether.shared_lib(b) {
        // source() defaults to <moduledir>.ae — ours is embed.ae.
        source("embed.ae")
        extra_source("_embed_support.c")
        output("libhtmlsanitizer.so")
    }
}
